"""NDJSON bridge for the Sophia Code macOS app (node-graph coding UI).

Unlike ``agent/app_bridge.py`` (one JSON payload per process spawn, used by the
reasoning-focused Sophia App), this bridge is a **long-lived line protocol**:

    python3 -m agent.code_bridge

stdin  — one JSON command per line:
    {"cmd": "config"}
    {"cmd": "run", "prompt": "...", "model": "mock", "mode": "balanced",
     "permission": "auto|manual|readonly", "session": "code-default",
     "deepThink": false, "team": 1, "skill": null, "cwd": null, "maxSteps": 12}
    {"cmd": "approve", "id": "ap-3", "allow": true}
    {"cmd": "cancel"}
     {"cmd": "sessions"} | {"cmd": "session_load", "session": "code-default"}
     {"cmd": "compound_workflow", "action": "run|resume|status|events|replay",
      "workflowCommandVersion": 1, "workflowRunKey": "stable-key", ...}
    {"cmd": "steer", "session": "code-default", "runId": "run-...", "prompt": "..."}
    {"cmd": "state"} | {"cmd": "settings", ...}
    {"cmd": "plugin", "action": "list|inspect|enable|disable|profile_use|..."}
    {"cmd": "shutdown"}

stdout — one JSON event per line:
    {"type": "ready", ...}
    {"type": "config" | "state" | "sessions", ...}
    {"type": "run_start" | "lane_start" | "lane_end" | "skill", ...}   (bridge events)
    {"type": "event", "runId": ..., "path": [...], "event": {...}}     (kernel events)
    {"type": "approval_request", "id": ..., "tool": ..., "preview": ...}
    {"type": "result", "runId": ..., "ok": ..., "certificate": {...}}
    {"type": "run_finished", "session": ..., "runId": ..., "ok": ..., "mode": ...}
    {"type": "error", ...}

Every kernel event (goal / thinking / tool_call / tool_result / final) is wrapped
with a ``path`` so the app can place it in the node graph: team lanes appear as
``lane-N`` frames and ``delegate`` subagents as ``sub-N`` frames. Token-level
streaming is emitted as ``{"type": "token"}`` bridge events when the transport
supports ``on_token`` (OpenAI-compatible + mock today).

Claim boundary: this is packaging/UX infrastructure only. Payloads force
``canClaimAGI: false``. Final-text handling follows the explicit Sophia Code
Conscience policy; external executable runtimes remain quarantined behind
Sophia's delivery floor.
"""
